Smart Environment Monitoring System using STM32 (DHT11 + LDR + OLED)
📌 Overview

This project implements a Smart Environment Monitoring System using an STM32 microcontroller. It measures temperature, humidity, and light intensity in real time using sensors and displays the results on an OLED screen. The system processes environmental data and categorizes conditions, enabling smart automation for homes and industries.

🎯 Features
Real-time monitoring of temperature and humidity
Ambient light detection using LDR
OLED display for live visualization
Multi-sensor integration
Compact embedded system design
🧠 Working Principle

The DHT11 sensor provides digital temperature and humidity data, while the LDR outputs an analog signal proportional to light intensity. The STM32 reads LDR values using ADC and DHT11 data via GPIO. The processed information is then displayed on an OLED using I2C communication.

🔧 Hardware Used
STM32 (e.g., STM32F4 series / Trainer Kit)
DHT11 Temperature & Humidity Sensor
LDR (Light Dependent Resistor)
SSD1306 OLED Display (I2C)
Connecting wires
🔌 Pin Configuration
Component	Pin
DHT11 Data	PA9
LDR (ADC Input)	PA0
I2C SCL	PB8
I2C SDA	PB9
⚙️ Software Configuration
IDE: STM32CubeIDE
Language: C (HAL Drivers)
ADC Resolution: 12-bit
Communication:
DHT11 → Single-wire protocol
OLED → I2C (SSD1306)
Timing: DWT-based microsecond delay
📊 Output

OLED displays:

TEMP  28C
HUM   65%
LIGHT BRIGHT

or

TEMP  25C
HUM   70%
LIGHT DARK
🚀 How It Works
ADC reads analog value from LDR
Light condition classified as DARK or BRIGHT
DHT11 sends temperature and humidity data
STM32 processes all sensor values
Data is formatted into readable strings
OLED displays updated information every second
▶️ How to Run
Open project in STM32CubeIDE
Build the project
Connect STM32 via ST-Link/USB
Flash the code
Observe real-time environmental data on OLED
⚠️ Notes
Use pull-up resistor (4.7k–10kΩ) for DHT11
Ensure correct OLED I2C address (0x3C or 0x78)
Adjust LDR threshold (ldr < 2000) based on environment
DWT must be enabled for accurate timing
Avoid noise in analog readings (use filtering if needed)
